# Vulnerabilities accepted with a reason.
#
# The scanner runs with `--ignore-unfixed`, so anything listed here has a fix
# available and is being accepted anyway. That is a higher bar than silence, and
# every entry needs a reason and a review date -- an ignore file without them is
# how a scanner becomes decoration.
#
# Nothing is listed today. The unfixable findings (perl-base and linux-libc-dev in
# the Debian bases, `ray` inside the upstream Airflow image) are excluded by
# `--ignore-unfixed` rather than enumerated here, because listing hundreds of CVEs
# nobody can act on would bury the ones that matter.
#
# Format: one CVE per line, with the reason above it. For example:
#
#   # CVE-0000-00000 -- reachable only through the C++ IPC reader, which the Python
#   # bindings do not expose. Review 2026-12-01.
#   CVE-0000-00000
